; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Castles -- Qal'alar: the kingdom's city and castle, the queen's dark castle,
; the ruined forts, and their halls. Six kits from Sketchfab, every one CC BY
; 4.0 (see CREDITS.md), cut into pieces by art/castles/export_castles.py.
;
; Not a biome and no depth's theme -- neither Biomes nor Themes lists it, so no
; floor strews a single piece (each PerHundred is 0). It is here so the map
; editor's scatter brush offers every piece by name, and a map or the world's
; writer names them from one place. A castle is built piece by piece on a map's
; Scenery, a piece a line: model[@picture] x y facing scale footprint|WxD
; [0xRRGGBB] (the engine's SceneryLine).
;
; FOOTPRINT: each Scatter says how a piece placed from it stands in the way. A
; wall is a box, WxD: W cells along its facing from its origin, D across it,
; centred -- at least 1.1 deep, so a wall on a grid line closes the cells on both
; sides of it. A tower, a column or a barrel is round, a radius in cells. A gate,
; an arch, a floor, a ramp or what hangs on a wall stands in nobody's way (0).
;
; THE QUEEN'S CASTLE: every fort piece is offered twice, as made and as
; model@picture with its _dark picture (models/buildings/fort/textures/*_dark.jpg):
; the same mesh, drawn darker, colder and a little red. A tint may go on top.
;
; ONE GRID: a cell is 10 units, the hero 12 tall; every piece is written at
; Scale 1 in those units. A WALL runs east from its origin along a grid line
; (facing 0; 90 north, 180 west, 270 south); a TOWER is centred on the grid
; point walls meet at; a FLOOR has its corner on a grid point and covers the
; cells east and south of it; a PROP is centred where it stands, at the height
; its kit gave it. Each kit's own module is in art/castles/export_castles.py:
;   rampart_*  towers every 5 cells, a 3-cell wall between, starting a cell
;              past the tower (maps/qasr is built of them)
;   fort_*     a wall 3 cells; each also @ its _dark picture, for the queen
;   town_*     the long wall 6 cells, the short 3.5; town_gate sits in
;              town_gatehouse placed at the same point and facing
;   hall_*     walls and floors 3 cells
;   desert_*   walls 3 cells, the blocks 2 and 4
;   room_*     walls 2 cells between column centres; the cornice at the same
;              point as its wall sits on top of it
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Theme
  Name = Castles
  ; Its own cells, should a floor ever be laid in it, are the keep's worked stone: see keep.duke.
  TileSize = 4
  WallHeight = 4
  WallShift = -0.5
  Stairs = models/terrain/dungeon/stairs.gltf
  CapTint = 0xA8A8B4
  StoreyShadePercent = 108
  FogTint = 0x07060A
  Tones = [
    Tone
      Name = Stone
      Floor = models/terrain/dungeon/floor.gltf
      Wall = models/terrain/dungeon/wall.gltf
    End
  ]
  ; Every piece, offered to the brush and strewn by nothing.
  Scenery = [
